[0.024, "o", "\r\n"]
[23.011, "o", "Fleet is fully healthy: all 3 managed clusters are available and joined, uniform version and size, with no platform add-ons deployed anywhere.\r\n\r\n| Cluster | Available | Joined | K8s Version | CPU | Memory | ClusterSet | Add-ons |\r\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\r\n| cluster1 | ✅ True | True | v1.30.4 | 4 | ~7.7 Gi | default | none |\r\n| cluster2 | ✅ True | True | v1.30.4 | 4 | ~7.7 Gi | default | none |\r\n| cluster3 | ✅ True | True | v1.30.4 | 4 | ~7.7 Gi | default | none |\r\n\r\n**Takeaways:** The fleet is perfectly homogeneous — 3/3 clusters available on v1.30.4 with identical 4-CPU / ~7.7 Gi capacity (12 CPU / ~23 Gi total), all in the `default` ClusterSet, so no version skew or drift to worry about. No add-ons are defined at the fleet level or installed on any cluster, so there's no add-on health risk — but also no observability/policy tooling deployed yet if you were expecting some.\r\n"]
[0.430, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[3.025, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# 5. PLACEMENT - where will new workloads land, and why?\u001b[0m\r\n"]
