[0.029, "o", "\r\n"]
[26.678, "o", "The hub rejected it. Per your instruction, I'm stopping here rather than reworking the manifests.\r\n\r\n**Refusal reason** — the proposal failed static guardrails on the Deployment (manifest 0), with eight violations:\r\n\r\n- `privileged=true` is not allowed\r\n- `allowPrivilegeEscalation` must be explicitly `false`\r\n- `runAsNonRoot` must be `true` (pod or container)\r\n- `runAsUser 0` (root) is not allowed\r\n- `capabilities.drop` must include `ALL`\r\n- `seccompProfile.type` must be `Localhost` or `RuntimeDefault`\r\n- `automountServiceAccountToken` must be explicitly `false` — \"an auto-mounted API token is a credential the workload does not need\"\r\n- image `nginx:latest` must be pinned — no `:latest`, no floating tags\r\n\r\nNothing was applied, and no proposal is sitting pending for approval. Worth noting that four of these (privileged, root, `:latest`, the service-account token) are inherent to the deployment as you described it, so this isn't a matter of adding missing boilerplate — a compliant version would have to"]
[0.000, "o", " run unprivileged as a non-root user on a digest-pinned image. Happy to draft that if you want it.\r\n"]
[0.440, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[3.021, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# 7. ship it RIGHT - the agent can only PROPOSE, never apply on its own\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.613, "o", "\u001b[1;32m$\u001b[0m "]
