[47.456, "o", "The proposal is created and pending approval — nothing has been applied.\r\n\r\n**Proposal ID: `4009080c0cdd48dea497a25ba6a1f899`**\r\n\r\nTo approve it, run `ocm-mcp approve 4009080c0cdd48dea497a25ba6a1f899` out-of-band and give me the token; only then can I apply it. I can't approve it myself.\r\n\r\nWhat's in the proposal: a single Deployment `storefront` in namespace `shop` on cluster2, 2 replicas of the pinned image `nginx:1.27.1`, port 80. The hub's guardrails and Kyverno policy rejected a plain non-privileged spec twice, so the final version carries the full Restricted profile they require: `automountServiceAccountToken: false`, and on the container `runAsNonRoot: true`, `privileged: false`, `allowPrivilegeEscalation: false`, all capabilities dropped, and a `RuntimeDefault` seccomp profile.\r\n\r\nOne caveat for the approver: the official `nginx:1.27.1` image starts as root by default, so with `runAsNonRoot: true` the kubelet may refuse to start the container at runtime (CreateContainerConfigError). If that happens "]
[0.000, "o", "after apply, the fix is to switch to `nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.27.1` (or set a non-root `runAsUser` and move the listen port off 80) in a follow-up proposal — but since the policy mandates runAsNonRoot, I kept the image exactly as you specified.\r\n"]
