[58.719, "o", "The proposal was applied successfully, but the storefront deployment is **not** coming up healthy — and I have the root cause.\r\n\r\n**What happened:**\r\n\r\n1. **Apply succeeded.** Proposal `4009080c…` matched the pending ManifestWork `storefront` (2 replicas of pinned `nginx:1.27.1` in namespace `shop` on cluster2, hardened pod spec), and `apply_manifestwork` returned `\"status\": \"applied\"`. The ManifestWork on the hub shows `Applied: True, Available: True` — the Deployment object itself was created on cluster2 without issue.\r\n\r\n2. **But the pods can't start.** Cluster health shows the deployment at **0/2 ready**, with both pods (`storefront-6b7d976446-n7kh5` and `-p42ct`) stuck Pending in `CreateContainerConfigError`. The events give the exact reason:\r\n\r\n   > `Error: container has runAsNonRoot and image will run as root (container: nginx)`\r\n\r\n**Root cause:** the hardened pod spec sets `runAsNonRoot: true`, but the stock `nginx:1.27.1` image runs as root (UID 0), so the kubelet refuses to start the container"]
[0.000, "o", ". This is deterministic, not transient — it will never become ready as-is. Notably, an earlier ReplicaSet (`storefront-88c564896`) failed 12 times with the identical error, so this same mismatch predates this proposal.\r\n\r\n**How to fix:** the cleanest option is a revised ManifestWork using a non-root nginx build, e.g. `nginxinc/nginx-unprivileged:1.27.1` (listens on 8080), or keep the stock image and set an explicit `runAsUser` with nginx configured for a non-root-compatible setup. Weakening the security context by dropping `runAsNonRoot` would work but defeats the hardening intent.\r\n\r\nSince any change needs a fresh proposal plus a human-minted approval token, tell me which direction you want (I'd recommend `nginx-unprivileged`) and I'll propose the corrected ManifestWork for you to approve with `ocm-mcp approve <id>`.\r\n"]
[0.370, "o", "\u001b[?25h"]
[3.020, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;36m# 10. the day, on the record - an operations log straight from the audit trail\u001b[0m\r\n"]
