[33.797, "o", "Operations log for this session, reconstructed from the tamper-evident audit trail (seq 1–16, all under operator `sandeepbazar`, 2026-07-28):\r\n\r\n- **Fleet review (seq 1–5):** Inventoried the fleet — listed managed clusters and hub-level ClusterManagementAddOns, then enumerated the enabled add-ons on each of cluster1, cluster2, and cluster3. All calls returned ok.\r\n- **Placement check (seq 6–7):** Read the PlacementDecision and full Placement spec for `demo-all` in namespace `default` to confirm which clusters the placement was selecting.\r\n- **Refused privileged request (seq 8):** A proposed `storefront` ManifestWork for cluster2 — nginx:latest running privileged, as UID 0, with privilege escalation allowed — was **rejected** by the guardrails and never reached a human approver. Two hardened follow-ups (seq 9–10) were also rejected until the pod spec fully satisfied policy.\r\n- **Approved storefront rollout (seq 11–13):** The compliant version passed validation — 2 replicas of pinned `nginx:1."]
[0.000, "o", "27.1` in namespace `shop`, runAsNonRoot, no privilege escalation, all capabilities dropped, RuntimeDefault seccomp, no service-account token. Proposal `4009080c…` was signed off by the human operator (`sandeepbazar`, who minted the approval token via `ocm-mcp approve`) and applied to cluster2.\r\n- **Verification (seq 14–16):** Post-apply checks read back the ManifestWork (Applied=True, Available=True, Deployment `shop/storefront` synced and available — still true as of just now), confirmed cluster2 health, and queried events in the `shop` namespace; no failures recorded.\r\n"]
